From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:07:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: let an idle-gated external DCP through
 a deep sleep

A T8132 external DCP with nothing attached is powered down after
dcpext_idle_ms. A deep sleep then calls iomfb_m4_ext_stop() for its
session, which returns -EALREADY for a DCP that is gated or stopped,
and the suspend fails with it: "dcp_platform_suspend returns -114".

Such a DCP is already down for the sleep, which is all the stop is
for, and its resume already takes the "off, nothing to replay" path.
Treat -EALREADY there as done.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 678b74dae7..b01480363d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -8251,6 +8251,9 @@ int iomfb_m4_suspend(struct apple_dcp *owner)
 
 			if (session)
 				ret = iomfb_m4_ext_stop(dcp);
+			/* Gated while idle, or stopped already: down for the sleep as it is. */
+			if (ret == -EALREADY)
+				ret = 0;
 		}
 		mutex_unlock(&dcp->lock);
 		return ret;
-- 
